 {"id": "DOC-2", "type": null, "priority": "P2", "status": "complete", "title": "doc rot: CONTRIBUTING.md dead pip extras install + wrong test counts + phantom test_integration.py + line-length mismatch", "description": null, "acceptance_criteria": null, "created_at": "2026-09-27T02:47:27+00:00", "created_by": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "5dbee9015b3690ce2ee5242b2e002069a1b08cf6e06997bc8debaa2ebc777843"}, "attempts": 0, "reasoning": "(a) CONTRIBUTING.md:9-12 `pip install -e \".[dev]\"` is a dead instruction: `[dev]` is a PEP 735 dependency-group (pyproject.toml:26-28, [dependency-groups]), not a pip extras section. Verified 2026-09-27: `pip install --dry-run -e '<repo>[dev]'` resolves to 'Would install PyYAML-6.0.3 terminal-jail-1.2.0' \u2014 pytest and ruff are NOT installed and the following setup steps fail. Correct path: `uv sync` (creates .venv with the dev group) or `pip install pyyaml pytest ruff==0.16.8`.\n(b) Test counts wrong 3 of 4 (pytest --collect-only via repo .venv, 2026-09-27): test_plugin.py '31 tests + 1 skipped' \u2192 actually 16 collected; test_install.py '11 tests' \u2192 66; test_standalone_cli.py '15 tests' \u2192 21; test_metrics_export.py '21' is correct.\n(c) CONTRIBUTING.md:62 lists plugin/test_integration.py in the project tree \u2014 the file does not exist (verified: `ls plugin/test_integration.py` \u2192 No such file or directory); integration coverage lives in plugin/test_env_scrub.py, plugin/test_escape_waves.py and friends.\n(d) CONTRIBUTING.md:48 'Line length: 100 characters' contradicts pyproject.toml:53 `line-length = 88`.\nreader: developer/contributor. accept: a fresh clone can follow CONTRIBUTING.md setup\u2192test\u2192lint with zero errors, and every test count in the file matches `pytest --collect-only`; regenerate counts from the collector, never from the docs.", "complexity": 3, "updated_at": "2026-09-27T13:40:00+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-27T13:29:46.594957+00:00", "commit_hash": "