+- id: TJ-DF-033
+  title: Wire metrics counters to plugin hooks
+  criteria:
+  - 'The Metrics dataclass in plugin/terminal_jail/plugin.py has 9 counters that are
+    never incremented outside tests. Add increment calls at the hook sites that already
+    fire: pre_tool_call/post_tool_call in plugin/__init__.py must increment commands_wrapped/commands_wrapped_user_ns/commands_passed_disabled/commands_passed_no_unshare
+    based on the mode and namespace outcome; jail_crashes increments when a sandboxed
+    command exits non-zero; byte_budget_rejections increments when the byte budget
+    check rejects; wrap_time_ns_total and wrap_count increment around the unshare
+    wrap; perf_regression_alert_count increments when a perf alert fires. Add a test
+    in plugin/test_metrics_counters.py that runs a real intercept() call and asserts
+    the counter incremented. Run .venv/bin/python -m pytest plugin/test_metrics_counters.py
+    -v and confirm it passes. Run scripts/metrics-export.py --json and confirm at
+    least one counter is non-zero after a real command.'
+  status: complete
+  created_at: '2026-09-30T04:57:44.837768+00:00'
+  completed_at: '2026-09-30T06:24:59.345890+00:00'
+- id: TJ-DF-034
+  title: Add --rule-pack-file path to install.sh
+  criteria:
+  - 'install.sh --rule-pack <name> only accepts packs shipped in plugin/terminal_jail/rules/packs/.
+    Add a new flag --rule-pack-file <path> that: (1) validates the pack with rule-pack-tool.py
+    validate <path>, (2) byte-copies it to the resolved rules dir (same destination
+    as --rule-pack), (3) adds a symmetric --uninstall-rule-pack-file <path> that removes
+    the installed copy. Document both flags in README.md under the rule-pack section.
+    Add a test in scripts/test_install.sh (or extend the existing install test) that
+    creates a temp pack file, installs it with --rule-pack-file, verifies it landed
+    in the rules dir, then uninstalls it. Run the test and confirm it passes.'
+  status: complete
+  created_at: '2026-09-30T04:57:45.352928+00:00'
+  completed_at: '2026-09-30T06:28:29.988461+00:00'
+- id: TJ-GAP-085
+  title: Expose rule resolution provenance in verdict
+  criteria:
+  - The engine returns rule_id and reason but not which layer won (engine builtin
+    vs shipped YAML mirror vs user rule dir vs rule pack). Add a 'layer' field to
+    InterceptResult (engine/yaml/user/pack) and populate it in Decider.evaluate()
+    based on which rule source matched. Update plugin/test_interruptor.py to assert
+    the layer field is present and correct for a builtin rule, a YAML mirror rule,
+    and a user rule. Update the JSON bridge output in plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_bridge.py
+    to include the layer field. Run .venv/bin/python -m pytest plugin/test_interruptor.py
+    -v and confirm all tests pass including the new layer assertions.
+  status: complete
+  created_at: '2026-09-30T04:57:45.860602+00:00'
+  completed_at: '2026-09-30T06:17:41.902767+00:00'
